  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PERFORMANCE-BASED PARTNERSHIP SCHEME FOCUSING ON QUALITY PROGRAMMING, UNDERSTANDING CHANGE AND RESULTS FOR POOR HOUSEHOLDS AND COMMUNITIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following a cholera outbreak in Gondor City and west Belesa woreda, Amhara, Ethiopia, Concern delivered a response to improve the capacity of health care providers in cholera case management and prevention. The project provided cholera case management training for health workers and cholera prevention training for health extension workers in both locations. To enhance public awareness on prevention of cholera cases, and promote social and behavioural change, extensive education sessions were conducted across the two woredas. .  OVERALL COUNTRY PROG: Contribute to immediate food and other essential commodities as well as reducing the risk of severe disease outbreak among fire affected persons..  SPECIFIC OUTCOME:</narrative>
  </description>
